{
  "purpose": "Handoff payload for bend2/scripts/laws-check.mjs MUTATIONS. Each entry replaces the first occurrence of a production-source string with a mutated one and is aimed at the named law when the isolated entry bend2/tests/context-core/laws-entry.bend is compiled. The operator boundary forbids local compilation; entries carried over from the pre-boundary baseline were refuted by their named law there, and every entry added or rewritten since is unexecuted.",
  "how_to_apply": "In a scratch copy of the pinned tree: for each entry, replace the first occurrence of `find` in `file` with `replace` (first-occurrence application and the operative law bytes are preserved); compile `entry` with the pinned bend 2.0.25; record the complete raw diagnostics and the process outcome. The verdict is NOT `the output contains the law name`: a type, syntax, launch or termination failure can name a law without refuting it. The single Controls/CI classifier decides, from the complete raw diagnostics and process outcome and from the expected/observed constructor metadata of the proof failure, whether this entry was refused by that law. Execution and classification belong to Controls/CI; this payload supplies the mutations and the law each one is aimed at, not an acceptance criterion.",
  "entry": "bend2/tests/context-core/laws-entry.bend",
  "dependency": "bend2/src/context/runtime/cdp-runtime.bend sha256 1dad59d15152728f48a65cfde470a5d10e555052fb2d53a41d64c8ec3c1e6368 (CDP 3ad9c12e, tree 6da63fa0). snapshot.bend and snapshot-laws.bend import it, so the composed tree must contain that exact file; this commit does not carry it.",
  "verified_baseline": "40e7060bf11ea1f8a924110e5a72815c9e343c41",
